tgies/klattsch @ 63dc2c6 (MIT), vendored with patches:
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [TR=ms] sets the formant transition into steady phonemes (default 35 ms, at most 40% of the phoneme; with TR, up to 90%)
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [AV=x] scales loudness (the synth's gain, default 3.5) and glides with the phoneme's transition
  src/engine/sequencer.js: a stop's bank entry may set burstMs (default 25 ms for all)
  src/engine/synth-core.js: shaped, per-parameter transitions: a schedule event may carry curve (1 raised cosine, 2 ease-out) and params
    (the parameters it moves; the others keep their own transitions); a schedule without either renders through the original code
  src/engine/sequencer.js: [TC=n] gives every event that curve; [CO=x] coarticulation: formants move in their own events, a vowel starts at
    and ends toward each neighbouring consonant's locus-equation value F + x (k F + c - F) ([COR=x] at VC; [COCV=ms], [COVC=ms]; [TCF=n]
    the formant events' curve), from bank fields vowel, locus {F1..F3: [k, c]}, locusVC, locusBurst (a stop's burst at the vowel's onset
    formants), transparent (HH: the next vowel's formants), smooth (liquids: no step); without [CO]/[TC] the schedule is unchanged
